1
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,650
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:10,600
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:14,430
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:17,370
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:21,410
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:29,420
I don't want to live
like this, buried in his dream...

7
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:35,270
You and Griffith...

8
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:40,900
I hope it works out between you and Griffith.

9
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:44,370
Hey.

10
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,240
Judeau, Corkus...

11
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:56,210
Come on, we need to talk.

12
00:01:06,130 --> 00:01:07,090
Griffith!

13
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,490
He would be able to stop him!

14
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:34,530
Feel no shame about shape

15
00:01:34,610 --> 00:01:36,450
Weather changes their phrase

16
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:40,200
Even mother will show you another way

17
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,580
So put your glasses on

18
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:44,660
Nothing will be wrong

19
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,870
There's no blame. There's no fame

20
00:01:46,870 --> 00:01:48,710
It's up to you

21
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:52,340
The first words should be found

22
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:55,970
Whatever holds you back

23
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:57,340
I...

24
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,470
...can...

25
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:00,640
I can get it off

26
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,640
Tell me what...

27
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,640
Tell me what...

28
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,470
Tell me what you want

29
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:05,560
I don't know why...

30
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:06,560
Don't know why...

31
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,560
Don't know why you're afraid

32
00:02:08,730 --> 00:02:09,730
Tell me what...

33
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:10,690
Tell me what...

34
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:12,360
Tell me what you'd say

35
00:02:12,610 --> 00:02:13,690
I don't know why...

36
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:14,780
Don't know why...

37
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:15,570
Too late...

38
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,190
It's too late

39
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:26,120
Separation

40
00:02:32,210 --> 00:02:34,750
What is this all of a sudden?

41
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:36,090
It's not sudden.

42
00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:39,130
I've been thinking about this since
before we set off for our last battle.

43
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:41,720
Are you discontent about something?

44
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:42,890
Of course I'm not...

45
00:02:42,890 --> 00:02:43,600
Not at all.

46
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:46,680
During these past three years....

47
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,520
...I've really enjoyed myself.

48
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:51,270
It's been like one great party.

49
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,360
How could I be discontent?

50
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:55,610
Oh, I didn't ask your name yet...

51
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:55,230
Then why do you...

52
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:57,940
Corkus, come on.

53
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:58,570
Shut up!

54
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:01,990
I am Sir Corkus, commander
of one of our companies!

55
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:05,990
What's wrong with me going
to a bar and hitting on a girl or two?

56
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:10,210
We've got free rein in any pub in Windham...

57
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:13,750
...once they recognize us as
Band of the Hawk commanders!

58
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:17,460
In the street, we're mobbed
by kids and women as we walk by!

59
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:18,800
Of course!

60
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,550
We are the heroes who saved this kingdom!

61
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:24,550
Soon, we'll be admitted
into society as nobles!

62
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:26,930
We'll be able to settle down in the court!

63
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:29,730
With luck, we could become
lords of our own castles!

64
00:03:29,730 --> 00:03:32,850
All of this would be impossible
under ordinary circumstances!

65
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:33,770
Right?

66
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:37,400
But we finally got our hands on it!

67
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,690
And it took a lot of blood,
sweat, and tears too!

68
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:43,950
And now you say you're
ready to throw it all away...

69
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,080
In any case...

70
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:50,540
Since killing people is your only talent...

71
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:54,000
...dancing at parties with
the ladies is probably beyond you!

72
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:56,590
What you say is true.

73
00:03:57,340 --> 00:04:01,550
I can't do anything but wield a sword.

74
00:04:06,510 --> 00:04:11,770
The first time I killed a man, I was
just a kid without a clue in the world.

75
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:16,020
I've never known anything but the battlefield.

76
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:17,610
I never tried to know more.

77
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,980
Killing others to survive...

78
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:21,610
That's all I've ever done.

79
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:22,780
But...

80
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:24,990
I could have been
content living that way...

81
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:26,620
If just one person...

82
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,280
Never mind who...

83
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:30,950
If only someone had
ever cared about me...

84
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,080
But...

85
00:04:36,130 --> 00:04:39,090
After wandering from one battlefield
to another, it finally hit me...

86
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:43,380
When it's kill or be killed, it doesn't
mean shit if someone cares or not.

87
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:46,470
Yearning for that is just childish.

88
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,510
Even so...

89
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,430
I ended up meeting him...

90
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:53,640
The one person
I desperately wanted to notice me.

91
00:04:58,190 --> 00:05:00,980
He had nothing whatsoever in his possession.

92
00:05:01,650 --> 00:05:04,190
And he was driven
to obtain everything.

93
00:05:06,570 --> 00:05:10,580
But because he aspires
to such great heights...

94
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:14,910
...his skills always have
to be honed to perfection.

95
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:20,590
And so he can't afford
to surround himself with the weak.

96
00:05:21,630 --> 00:05:25,090
But the funny thing is
the more I see him in that light...

97
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:27,430
...the more dazzling he seems to me.

98
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:36,640
I've had enough of it. Being part of
his dream, always looking up at him.

99
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:43,530
I want to achieve a goal of my own,
so that I can call myself his equal.

100
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:48,280
He's the one man I can't
have looking down on me.

101
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:51,410
Call yourself Griffith's equal, huh?

102
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,750
Cut the crap!

103
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:56,910
That's what you call childish bullshit!

104
00:05:56,910 --> 00:05:58,540
He's special, don't you see?

105
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,250
He's not like the rest of us!

106
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,750
You have no talent but slaying people...

107
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:05,960
Yet here you are, way out of your
class, as our raider commander...

108
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:08,590
And you have no one
to thank for that but Griffith!

109
00:06:08,590 --> 00:06:11,220
I have no interest in rank or position.

110
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,890
It's something else that I'm after...

111
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:16,140
Something I have
to claim with my own hands.

112
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:19,440
That's what I mean by childish drivel!

113
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:21,690
Something you have
to claim with your own hands?

114
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:25,650
Life would be a lot easier
if we could all find such a thing!

115
00:06:25,650 --> 00:06:26,650
Listen!

116
00:06:26,650 --> 00:06:31,120
We all have to make compromises
in life, depending on our limitations...

117
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,370
...and the cards that
we're dealt in this world!

118
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:36,620
People who think
that all they need is a dream...

119
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:38,370
You guys make me sick!

120
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:43,380
That's nothing but an excuse
for cowards who can't face reality!

121
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:44,290
Corkus...

122
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:47,050
What about you?

123
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,300
Isn't there something
you want to claim too?

124
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:54,260
Gimme a break!

125
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,930
I need to get some sleep!

126
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,980
I can't tolerate this
immature fool any longer!

127
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:07,780
That Corkus... He may not look it, but
he was once a band of thieves' leader.

128
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:13,780
I suppose at one point, he did have
something that he wanted to claim...

129
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:15,700
...with his own hands, like you.

130
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:19,120
As for myself...

131
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:22,500
I've always been proficient
at anything I set my mind to.

132
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,720
My quick wit and skills with a knife
have always been superior to most.

133
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:35,050
But I could never be
the best at any one thing.

134
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:38,600
That's why I decided...
If I couldn't be the best...

135
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,520
...then I would serve
under someone who could.

136
00:07:42,770 --> 00:07:45,770
I think everyone has
the desire to attain something...

137
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:50,740
I'll see you out...

138
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:54,950
I hope you find it...
That something you're after...

139
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,290
Hey, Guts...

140
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:03,040
Yeah?

141
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:05,830
Why don't you ask Casca to go with you?

142
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:06,340
What?

143
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:08,130
What are you talking about?

144
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:11,720
As if it wasn't obvious enough
already. Griffith's the one she...

145
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:15,930
I don't think Casca can ever be with Griffith.

146
00:08:15,930 --> 00:08:16,680
Why?

147
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:20,390
Because there's only one
thing that Griffith is after...

148
00:08:21,230 --> 00:08:25,980
And winning Princess Charlotte's
hand is the fastest shortcut to it.

149
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:28,190
And it's the only way he can ever hope to.

150
00:08:29,230 --> 00:08:32,570
Anyway, what do you think of Casca?

151
00:08:34,150 --> 00:08:36,820
Sure, I think Casca's attractive.

152
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:41,250
There aren't a lot of women you can
trust your back to on the battlefield.

153
00:08:42,450 --> 00:08:45,960
But I don't really see Casca as a woman...

154
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,290
She's more like my comrade-in-arms.

155
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:48,960
Well, then...

156
00:08:55,510 --> 00:08:56,180
No...

157
00:08:57,300 --> 00:08:58,390
...you're wrong.

158
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:02,390
She only has eyes for Griffith.

159
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:06,230
So for now, I can't be the one for her.

160
00:09:08,610 --> 00:09:09,690
I see.

161
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:14,190
I guess I was the only one who
thought there was some hope for you.

162
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:21,910
Thanks for coming along.
I'll be off now...

163
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Guts!

164
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:30,380
You...

165
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:33,210
You're so mean. How could
you leave without saying anything?

166
00:09:33,710 --> 00:09:36,800
Why? Are you tired
of the Band of the Hawk?

167
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:37,800
Rickert...

168
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:51,440
Are you leaving?

169
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,320
Yeah...

170
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:55,440
Are you resigning from
the Band of the Hawk?

171
00:09:56,650 --> 00:09:57,900
Sorry...

172
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,200
You're sorry?
That doesn't explain anything!

173
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,700
You've got to tell us why!

174
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:05,950
The Band of the Hawk is like
your own family! Isn't that true?

175
00:10:06,370 --> 00:10:08,000
Stop it, Rickert.

176
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,960
Why...

177
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,670
It's a man's decision.

178
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:12,670
We should just let him go.

179
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:15,840
But Guts is the commander of the Raiders!

180
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:17,800
He's crucial to the Band of the Hawk!

181
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:21,760
We were already invincible before he joined.

182
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,680
But...

183
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:23,470
Shut up!

184
00:10:25,970 --> 00:10:28,350
Hey, I'm going to tell you this now!

185
00:10:28,690 --> 00:10:30,900
I've always hated you!

186
00:10:31,310 --> 00:10:32,940
I'll never acknowledge your skills!

187
00:10:33,230 --> 00:10:35,360
You're not special at all!

188
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:38,820
And you'll never be like Griffith!

189
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:43,530
If we ever meet on the battlefield someday...

190
00:10:43,830 --> 00:10:45,790
...you'd better watch your back!

191
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:51,630
Guts...

192
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,590
Thanks for everything...

193
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:22,700
I told you this long ago...

194
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:25,200
You belong to me.

195
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:38,550
I claimed you with this sword of mine.

196
00:11:39,340 --> 00:11:43,430
When to go into battle,
when to die... that is all up to me.

197
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:46,810
If you want to free
yourself from my control...

198
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,640
...then just as you did before...

199
00:11:49,060 --> 00:11:50,890
Wrest yourself away with your blade!

200
00:11:51,390 --> 00:11:52,480
Griffith!

201
00:11:52,850 --> 00:11:55,940
You can't just let me go
with a smile and "goodbye," huh?

202
00:11:59,650 --> 00:12:00,780
I see.

203
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,040
Wait!

204
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,500
Are you two serious?

205
00:12:11,910 --> 00:12:14,080
You're going to cross swords
even though you're comrades?

206
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,300
Stay back, Casca!

207
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,090
Get out of the way.

208
00:12:22,090 --> 00:12:23,470
What are you saying?

209
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:26,300
If you two fight with real swords,
you won't escape unharmed!

210
00:12:27,930 --> 00:12:29,850
Hands off! What are you doing?

211
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:32,350
There's no way around it,
under these circumstances...

212
00:12:34,060 --> 00:12:35,690
What are you all doing?

213
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:37,270
We've got to stop them!
They'll kill each other!

214
00:12:37,610 --> 00:12:39,320
This is between the two of them.

215
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:41,490
It's not our place to interfere.

216
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:44,030
But we can't just...

217
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:46,950
Have you gotten so used to
the genteel life that you've forgotten?

218
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:50,240
We must settle things by our swords.

219
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:52,410
This is our way as mercenaries, isn't it?

220
00:12:53,210 --> 00:12:54,160
But...

221
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:57,080
She's changed...

222
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,960
She's never hesitated before
under Griffith's orders...

223
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:02,630
...even if her comrades
were in mortal danger.

224
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:06,680
Does she realize it herself?
That she's starting to change?

225
00:13:12,810 --> 00:13:15,190
His eyes look as if he's glaring at an enemy.

226
00:13:16,390 --> 00:13:17,230
But...

227
00:13:17,850 --> 00:13:21,820
...even if he hates me
or if he considers me a traitor...

228
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:25,400
I'm still going!

229
00:13:29,570 --> 00:13:31,910
It's just as it was three years ago...

230
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:35,790
It all began with a sword fight...
and it will end with a sword fight.

231
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:38,170
I'm proud that I've come this far...

232
00:13:39,210 --> 00:13:42,630
The fact you're challenging me
now shows I'm valuable enough...

233
00:13:43,090 --> 00:13:44,970
...for you to shed blood for.

234
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,590
He's become immeasurably strong...

235
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:51,010
But...

236
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:54,430
Griffith can definitely stop him!

237
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:59,310
That's right. Then everything will
be the same as it was before...

238
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:03,190
Is that my wish?

239
00:14:03,610 --> 00:14:05,240
Is it my wish that...

240
00:14:07,030 --> 00:14:09,200
...Guts stays with me?

241
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:17,790
He makes no attempt
to display his will to fight.

242
00:14:18,710 --> 00:14:20,630
However, he is completely on guard...

243
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,500
...and his eyes are resolute.

244
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:28,380
Do you really wish so much...

245
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:30,890
...to be free of my control?

246
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:33,310
No, I won't allow it!

247
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:36,770
My best chance is in the first strike...

248
00:14:36,770 --> 00:14:39,640
I've got to deflect his sword
as soon as he swings downward.

249
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,310
Then I'll strike his shoulder!

250
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:46,070
If my sword strays the least bit off
the mark, I could end up killing him.

251
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:51,280
Nevertheless, if I can't make him mine...

252
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:52,450
I don't care!

253
00:15:08,170 --> 00:15:08,670
Now!

254
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,330
Griffith!

255
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:52,680
Goodbye.

256
00:16:00,310 --> 00:16:01,560
Griffith...

257
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:25,830
Guts!

258
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:41,980
Guts is gone.
He didn't even look back.

259
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,060
That was a fluke!

260
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:44,600
That was definitely a fluke!

261
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:46,310
I'll never admit that he won!

262
00:16:51,690 --> 00:16:52,940
You're going to be all right...

263
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:56,570
It's like you just stumbled
over a stone in the street.

264
00:16:57,370 --> 00:16:59,080
It's not a big deal at all...

265
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:04,660
The place you're headed...
It's far beyond this, right?

266
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:07,960
You'll be fine...
You'll get back on your feet...

267
00:17:08,790 --> 00:17:11,760
...and start walking again...
before you know it.

268
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,350
No, the snow is melting...

269
00:17:28,900 --> 00:17:33,530
Please go to bed quickly,
otherwise you will get sick, my lady.

270
00:17:33,530 --> 00:17:34,780
Fine, I shall retire now.

271
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:36,650
You may leave now.

272
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:38,490
Then good night, my lady.

273
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:56,760
Sir Griffith!

274
00:17:58,470 --> 00:18:00,850
Sir Griffith, what happened to you?

275
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:03,470
It's such a rainy night!

276
00:18:03,470 --> 00:18:05,930
Good evening, Princess Charlotte.

277
00:18:06,350 --> 00:18:09,400
May I be so bold as to request
entry into your chambers?

278
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,150
What?

279
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:14,650
If someone saw us like this,
it might stain your honor, Princess.

280
00:18:15,110 --> 00:18:16,400
Y-Yes...

281
00:18:17,950 --> 00:18:19,110
Come in...

282
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:19,910
Thank you.

283
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:24,240
Please excuse my rudeness,
visiting a lady's bedroom...

284
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:27,750
...at such a late hour
and soaking the place with rain.

285
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:32,920
I missed you so much.

286
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:36,010
Ever since you were sent to the battlefield...

287
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:39,510
...I have constantly been afraid
that I would hear of your death.

288
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:43,640
Even after you returned, so many
terrifying and tragic things occurred!

289
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:49,350
Why... Why didn't you
come to see me earlier?

290
00:19:00,530 --> 00:19:01,450
No...

291
00:19:12,420 --> 00:19:13,920
Griffith...

292
00:19:16,090 --> 00:19:17,670
Griffith!

293
00:19:18,760 --> 00:19:20,300
Are you scared?

294
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:24,680
Stop it...

295
00:19:25,390 --> 00:19:31,440
Your fear and sorrow... Throw
everything into the fire and let it burn...

296
00:20:41,420 --> 00:20:42,630
Goodbye...

297
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:01,900
Griffith?

298
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:24,130
Well, well, who should it be
but the next White Hawk general!

299
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:28,590
To think that Your Excellency, of
all people, should be here at this time.

300
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,520
That's right. My sword was...

301
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:36,270
I will hear your story later, at my leisure.

302
00:21:36,810 --> 00:21:37,850
Haul him off!

303
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

304
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

305
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

306
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

307
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

308
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

309
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

310
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

311
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

312
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

313
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

